bes the region bounded by the inequality $5x-10y<-20?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-10y & <-20 \\\\ -10y & <-5x-20 \\\\ 10y & >5x+20 \\\\ y & >\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2.$ Since the inequality involves a 'strictly greater than' sign, the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y>\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/351bb4b4324432e2cc747e67dac22100da3c9e5318339832efa046f504394c35.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109942/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9ceefc-3aa8-5c13-90a1-e4a084f720cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109942"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64023/selection/90f00e10e185fdd0376c61504ec52cb8063e0ea581a31eaee00bffcc093d0884" :answer/id #uuid "c2c7c168-866b-50a6-8068-09b87d0d5f0c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/baba27c5989981679ac5e5290db3b88803f892659869b54991b17a0b1574e422.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64023/selection/c4fa52bb5626cf3d2952a2a177bef786bafd4a9cf5a70f63b2ce5d3ad1a3ef67" :answer/id #uuid "7913228d-237a-5aa3-b357-25262c48890b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/a50effb3acd9884ab7f351a820720a0a3ab7728c9242c576a17ddc58ad2d7111.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64023/sel