id "q-64023" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $x-y>-5?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & >-5 \\\\ -y & >-x-5 \\\\ y & <x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=x+5.$ Since the inequality involves a 'strictly less than' sign, the line $y=x+5$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y<x+5$ refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line $y=x+5,$ so we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/bd0ce52fe5aaf5e95c4f2eb5bd14652ee696c7bb2dfdb99ccdf07543be46f45e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64023/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9ceefc-3aa8-5c13-90a1-e4a084f720cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64023"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142113/selection/d513bd41e02896224d08a3237bc0ffac94b78ea772795508173b27e29f5866b5" :answer/id #uuid "54e5ec57-bac5-5cca-971c-8ae35bf37d08" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/5f7df5dc434ecc1a04fc60aa476303db2ccea9dda6b8a9fa28eae5dedddc44b6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142113/selection/94f07f3055f8743f64beddd679a4a9f2e23c1b39f1eddb5caacc9ce8331938b2" :answer/id #uuid "8d9c1cac-5995-595a-8ef2-04e50db59b74" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/35e2d168ece734f2bc84a3b9c41208cb941fabbf8b4c9b1de600f8c5dad5ac1d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142113/selection/bd5139745597fdf3d6589694ddc83dc377fee3c9a9bd08ba8d42fb23d19375c9" :answer/id #uuid "4aa3ca47-844b-5023-9f52-4e8e676b34e9" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/2a46c79189ad438d1c4bd1528e50e93881bbf7690d37b16b9ebeaaa44bff06a8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142113/selection/8d0402caa1292d09c4516ebf000d52d5819512ef4c5ac8dbc11ffcb6af68a56a" :answer/id #uuid "b6684340-75bf-50f2-8dbd-b881f1f05820" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/8e7f4a75c7793e4770643cc40decbfd007f7809f96475a914c5c00d4f5ee13bc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142113/selection/308c5e6e066f6787a617e4af7f2fc3fc1d636e5d15ce091fe6d9adc65cb8155a" :answer/id #uuid "da2d4eba-9681-5c20-aa56-5bc930b166e3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/5456e2ee349d219f3072d305415c939d5d4a3b0cbc189b55be3102fb5c72a3a7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142113/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3af5ebc-bf75-5ada-b49a-3e620b7e319e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142113/selection/8d0402caa1292d09c4516ebf000d52d5819512ef4c5ac8dbc11ffcb6af68a56a" :answer-field/choices ["q-142113/selection/d513bd41e02896224d08a3237bc0ffac94b78ea772795508173b27e29f5866b5" "q-142113/selection/94f07f3055f8743f64beddd679a4a9f2e23c1b39f1eddb5caacc9ce8331938b2" "q-142113/selection/bd5139745597fdf3d6589694ddc83dc377fee3c9a9bd08ba8d42fb23d19375c9" "q-142113/selection/8d0402caa1292d09c4516ebf000d52d5819512ef4c5ac8dbc11ffcb6af68a56a" "q-142113/selection/308c5e6e066f6787a617e4af7f2fc3fc1d636e5d15ce091fe6d9adc65cb8155a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142113" :question/id #uuid "6025b073-9e75-57a3-a820-ad415f72c95d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142113" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $2x+4y\\ge 8?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y & \\ge 8 \\\\ 4y & \\ge -2x+8 \\\\ y & \\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'greater than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **solid line**.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/226415c7de8240eaa2a87a10e87d95c6dbf45df6263c4b36ea819cfec097a8a0.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142113/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "031f0fd6-385d-56b8-9e8e-b264e6e89ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142112/selection/f6cdb2f8102ecf2adcd3864c3e2e1e7088b07e845bb3aa39da0b20b2eb47c237" :answer/id #uuid "d83b2117-eed4-587c-b968-e2d2c35cf69b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/1a8b3896667e3401eb610625ee71607c221ad7cdaf2d4ccea79bdbe54665ec7e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142112/selection/8544ada6da7ec396c2b71aae0ac9f03e1745da3d2fbd5177155b0210d8ca05a5" :answer/id #uuid "1e623676-cb74-580b-aacf-53c3433c615d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/ec99abbe475fc356cfd