d/validate]} {:db/id "q-142112" :question/id #uuid "60ebcac8-bc59-5dde-9394-be5d3c916d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-142112" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $x+2y\\le 4?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & \\le 4 \\\\ 2y & \\le -x+4 \\\\ y & \\le -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'less than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **solid line**. \n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny\\le -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2,$ so we shade *below* the line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/8b906cf167528f484109528a93732dc2b8d73558bb02f454bb520af87efde3c5.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142112/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "031f0fd6-385d-56b8-9e8e-b264e6e89ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142112"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109946/selection/752b6f95f75c13a574f4692b3aadbf9d9ee16f76335bc313beb2be1cd3cc8538" :answer/id #uuid "57547bda-e94c-5c99-b1b7-5cdac989b549" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/8104d0507b16ac8c43900e8278e8d5079f99539b56c9eb150b938751d6c57810.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109946/selection/f6b4b1271ee1a5887900d03ce718f6cadfbe02759a4cae403c58049c74141bbc" :answer/id #uuid "f1c154f6-233f-501f-b572-e870f1aea62a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/