9947" "q-109946/selection/cb66904e0681e2b4fd04ffccde016ba323bc38f6382dde6251ff07e90c2fc16d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109946" :question/id #uuid "8fc6e780-0a9e-5665-a2f1-8e50997d5b65" :question/math-academy-id "q-109946" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $2x-y\\ge 3?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y & \\ge 3 \\\\ -y & \\ge -2x+3 \\\\ y & \\le 2x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=2x-3.$ Since the inequality involves a 'less than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=2x-3$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a solid line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y\\le 2x-3$ refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line $y=2x-3,$ so we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/020b2d81ed5913dfe41fb296811da30ee2c6ea4fc7ea8184335db6d866598c5a.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109946/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "031f0fd6-385d-56b8-9e8e-b264e6e89ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143098/selection/bf0bf2d08583b9053496f1b4a2ffbf597f8b9e8af560a7e246a2c84eabfbf9b7" :answer/id #uuid "f0f5c518-1a5d-523a-931b-6ea2f80c44a2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/f18b75a1d71e01bd898e14a66bbec923abd988c72a8e9d69451c8edf1d16fc72.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143098/selection/ba7873752cfbfe84656cc29e7175f4ee7e91676fba1c1a3689504122f9005f1d" :answer/id #uuid "b89782c6-cc02-53c5-8e64-aee8a066915e" :answer/type