95b6da4bec203a789a19296cd9b97b13" "q-143098/selection/6ab8c4880e43903372ba716e382f472d035f588f783bead7a0af8a21398b966a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143098" :question/id #uuid "ea4847f7-e663-5fb5-abcf-705c57877607" :question/math-academy-id "q-143098" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $3x-2y\\ge 6?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y & \\ge 6 \\\\ -2y & \\ge -3x+6 \\\\ y & \\le \\frac{3}{2}x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{2}x-3.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'less than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-3$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **solid line**.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{3}{2}x-3\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-3,$ so we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/ea12ed8d62304ecdc90859d5cd206045cef852522ce16c67a9307ddbd755b3dc.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143098/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "031f0fd6-385d-56b8-9e8e-b264e6e89ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143098"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109940/selection/5e6df636e284bc8c09ef3c8b2687a54cb3aa98d0b76ce968c94e05fa5efb4554" :answer/id #uuid "ce553c50-eee6-5849-a160-0b18133622f9" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/2ae1370dda61376a0c8b684a33f3722620aef05ee289f0a83591546e49221389.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109940/selection/f9c9512fde8277b2