* those on the line $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx>-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-214907/field-1" "q-214907/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-214907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-44558/selection/52bc76e880d56692149fad05b0e295fb06e498cebb7be55a6dfade2cee21ef0b" :answer/id #uuid "0c57c29f-e8df-5b13-ae84-409da2fb7177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44558/selection/bec3bf80e36fca8f0b4926ff5c3a771336556280e9f9e11880b332377e3740f4" :answer/id #uuid "01ad819b-aa4f-595b-bc07-9ea5de110c5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44558/selection/8ef4120686e7520d69cb1d7684d905708092536316e2305259fdf82e491966ae" :answer/id #uuid "518cae7a-9824-53c4-a09f-077f9223ee9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44558/selection/72d37d0e9e217c6dedd80716653dc2c090afad1dde2d4c1088cc12071ca95645" :answer/id #uuid "19c83f6f-5be1-58b6-b4f8-fa2a93e8008a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y>x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44558/selection/1235061e5472926481ddeb36b23313e44d3189b3ae0ecc652c6bbec56a95bfe7" :answer/id #uuid "af7af458-acee-5de8-9a35-a2daeafc2fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44558/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "080641ca-4845-5e66-b1f3-ef1302b7f255" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-44558/selection/bec3bf80e36fca8f0b4926ff5c3a771336556280e9f9e11880b332377e3740f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-44558/selection/52bc76e880d56692149fad05b0e295fb06e498cebb7be55a6dfade2cee21ef0b" "q-44558/selection/bec3bf80e36fca8f0b4926ff5c3a771336556280e9f9e11880b332377e3740f4" "q-44558/selection/8ef4120686e7520d69cb1d7684d905708092536316e2305259fdf82e491966ae" "q-44558/selection/72d37d0e9e217c6dedd80716653dc2c090afad1dde2d4c1088cc12071ca95645" "q-44558/selection/1235061e5472926481ddeb36b23313e44d3189b3ae0ecc652c6bbec56a95bfe7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-44558" :question/id #uuid "4ef15986-247a-5c73-9a2b-17e3295a31c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44558" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/daa0365127a12a9a561d0790af855b5f26f8ab9188ac541b142cd9d9e0a919cc.png)\n\nFind the inequality that describes the shaded region shown above." :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a horizontal line passing through the point $(0,2).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $y=2.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is solid, we will use an \"or equal to\" inequality. Since the shaded region is *above* the line, the inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than or equal to* those on the line $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-44558/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-44558"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-1/85abe6323fb17d3528cb41e333e484a220f40de73de0ade5b121284eb6b9769f" :answer/id #uuid "8fb71d81-bcee-5ace-a028-62e2e6f1ddce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer/id #uuid "95dcee54-b96f-5308-81f7-afb17d874eb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf57dc5e-d5bb-5281-b90d-7fd527085eb8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-215437/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer-field/choices ["q-215437/field-1/85abe6323fb17d3528cb41e333e484a220f40de73de0ade5b121284eb6b9769f" "q-215437/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-2/914a4c635b27937a50bc7cd07e667cc9a4a79ecfa28a5337e1ae972f164f8e5e" :answer/id #uuid "5c8e42a3-1add-517d-b9ac-37eeca9742c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-2/1a674f984a743f5373d07776898fdafa3a8deeddb94203f1ccfbc07d525d6d38" :answer/id #uuid "653c80fa-84ab-56da-9f98-3fd929c51418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-2/b474c84d7ad00d9ee145944549d7221a4cbd214ace62f3c5023f6dd7b4eb239e" :answer/id #uuid "df0aa774-6fa5-5c84-b14f-3e3a425535c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-2/c5c8d6cecfbc22709fa6fa62a5f2c9ff8595dacbf2ed74115e76dca0241e3adb" :answer/id #uuid "5347ab2d-c782-59b1-b304-fe8e36592d7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4a1cc2b-0033-5b6a-9965-67bc756f6dd9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-215437/field-2/b474c84d7ad00d9ee145944549d7221a4cbd214ace62f3c5023f6dd7b4eb239e" :answer-field/choices ["q-215437/field-2/914a4c635b27937a50bc7cd07e667cc9a4a79ecfa28a5337e1ae972f164f8e5e" "q-215437/field-2/1a674f984a743f5373d07776898fdafa3a8deeddb94203f1ccfbc07d525d6d38" "q-215437/field-2/b474c84d7ad00d9ee145944549d7221a4cbd214ace62f3c5023f6dd7b4eb239e" "q-215437/field-2/c5c8d6cecfbc22709fa6fa62a5f2c9ff8595dacbf2ed74115e76dca0241e3adb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215437" :question/id #uuid "84d30d8f-6033-5842-95cc-601ebb4c6d51" :question/math-academy-id "q-215437" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/bb24be727a3bb001e25b5f2c758b1302332aa8b45a51cfd0d4884b2784479e58.png)\n\nExpress the shaded region above as an inequality.\nThe shaded region above is described by the inequality\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-1,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $x=-1.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is solid, we will use an \"or equal\" inequality. Since the shaded region is to the *left* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *less than or equal to* those on the line $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx\\le -1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215437/field-1" "q-215437/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-29423"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/dcfffb2c9005da34a529cdf5ef372bdac840a1308b92507ad0ea0a5359a1387f.png)\n\nFind the inequality that describes the shaded region shown above." :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-4,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $x=-4.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is to the *right* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $x=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx>-4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14041"] :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & <4 \\\\ 2y & <-x+4 \\\\ y & <-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves a 'strictly less than' sign, the line $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n\nThen, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny < -\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\nrefers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line $y = -\\dfrac{1}{2}x+2,$ so we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/1450257c533c670d3ce0d803aa62b75c2ffe44159e26a3daf5dd3c04026a6fe4.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14047"] :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-y & \\le -1 \\\\ -y & \\le x-1 \\\\ y & \\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=-x+1.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'greater than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=-x+1$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a *solid line*.\n\nThen, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny \\geq -x+1\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line $y=-x+1,$ so we shade *above* the line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/a649958285f52e9d61c665bf4cd58844e4ed7cea1cf9e0f949efe5a0f25e3263.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14056"] :question/problem "Find the inequality that describes the shaded region shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/677e2257e2cb3a5706b7dc2d1088fc68ff12a2c39d976819d52f25fb2dfbe77d.png)" :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-1,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation \n\n$$\nx=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. \n\n- Since the line is *dashed*, we will use a *strict* inequality.\n\n- Since the shaded region is to the *right* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx > -1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
